09151932001-cea2e5e9-969b-44d2-a309-33c1893d8b56"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b6e5c9b58f9f1feaed8f6d96a71b3da8ff28fe266e4efc06b997a63d1848ec68","event_uuid":"53559e41-ba40-4b0c-ac1b-607808ed3467","position":{"commit_sha":"609cb0ff0b5b70437d002ad9cf27e4bc4a1fbd47","position":"1785808032983907001-53559e41-ba40-4b0c-ac1b-607808ed3467"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7e052b7ab34be4532dc75e81b2fe4c85f7d9f686f7b7000b272559f7572a9a0b","event_uuid":"a3120576-9780-47ed-ad93-94ac4cd76334","position":{"commit_sha":"609cb0ff0b5b70437d002ad9cf27e4bc4a1fbd47","position":"1785808034101120001-a3120576-9780-47ed-ad93-94ac4cd76334"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1785807684044955001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"19ec0f43-1860-4e30-9a1a-efda37c3da70","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"d37e-4f64-3265-4f30"},{"link_uuid":"f20b723f-c883-41d2-b805-779e81f1c7ad","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"1e95-fc5c-bca8-44c7"}],"description":"# New-gate CI steps fail pre-gate changes: workflow from target branch, tree from change\n\n## Summary\n\nGerrit's verify job takes the **workflow definition from the target branch** but **checks out the change's tree**. A newly landed gate step that runs a repo script (`python scripts/check_X.py`) therefore hard-fails every open change whose base predates the gate-introducing commit: the step runs, but the script does not exist in the checked-out tree.\n\nObserved in production: changes 1332/1333 (based before d37e's 6739ea54fa landed) failed Verified with `python: can't open file '.../scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory`. The just-merged wall-clock-assert gate (1e95, 9af88c3ada, scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py) has the identical window. Immediate recovery for 1332/1333 was a server-side rebase:chain — but every future gate-script landing re-opens this window for all in-flight changes.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe two new gate steps in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml invoke their script unconditionally. The workflow definition and the checked-out tree can legitimately diverge (definition-from-target-branch is Gerrit CI's model), so a gate step must tolerate a tree that predates its script.\n\n## Fix plan\n\nGuard both new gate steps with an existence check that SKIPS (with an explanatory log line) when the script is absent from the checked-out tree:\n\n    - name: raw-git-write gate\n      run: |\n        if [ -f scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py ]; then\n          python scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py\n        else\n          echo \"scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py not in checked-out tree (change predates the gate) — skipping\"\n        fi\n\nSame shape for the wall-clock-assert gate step. Include an inline workflow comment stating the idiom and WHY (definition-from-target-branch vs change tree skew), so future gate authors copy the guard along with the step. Deleting a gate script in a change silently skips that gate for that change — acceptable: such a deletion is itself visible in review, and the gate re-enforces on every post-merge change.\n\nOlder gate steps (comment-hygiene, module-size, commit wrap) predate all open changes; leave them unguarded to keep the diff minimal — the documented idiom covers any future script.\n\n## Verification\n\n- actionlint via make lint passes on the edited workflow.\n- Shell logic locally exercised both branches: script present -> runs detector (exit propagates); script absent (temp dir) -> skip message, exit 0.\n- CI on the change itself (which HAS both scripts) still runs both gates — Verified +1 proves the present-branch path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Both new gate steps (raw-git-write, wall-clock-assert) skip with an explanatory message when their script is absent from the checked-out tree, and run it when present.\n- [ ] The skew rationale + copy-me idiom is documented inline in the workflow at the gate steps.\n- [ ] make lint (actionlint) passes; both branches of the guard exercised locally.\n\n## File impact\n\n- .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml (edit)","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"guard both new gate steps with script-existence check + document the skew idiom"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"53559e41-ba40-4b0c-ac1b-607808ed3467","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ee2a-c7d7-3d73-425e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"New-gate CI steps fail pre-gate changes: workflow from target branch, tree from change","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e8d0374a-3ee5-42c9-97bf-008070314445","15dca8af-7780-40f3-82b0-5d7da15a8ae0","19ec0f43-1860-4e30-9a1a-efda37c3da70","f20b723f-c883-41d2-b805-779e81f1c7ad","cea2e5e9-969b-44d2-a309-33c1893d8b56","53559e41-ba4